    <div class="bu-layouts">
      <figure class="panel"><div class="bu-mock phone"><i class="rail l"></i><i class="map"></i><i class="rail r"></i></div><figcaption><b>Phone cockpit</b>Landscape + full screen gates. Left rail: menu, pause, readouts, Command, camera, stick. Right rail: orders, Auto, Lock, Fire. Notch-safe; Command slides the right rail away and Fire becomes a small ✕.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="panel"><div class="bu-mock desk"><i class="head"></i><i class="map"></i><i class="bar"></i></div><figcaption><b>Desktop bar</b>RADIO (Command) · RADIO · WHOLE SQUAD · PLATOON · RADIOS (centre) · AIM · Surrender far right. Labels when it all fits on one line.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="panel"><div class="bu-mock compact"><i class="head"></i><i class="map"></i><i class="bar"></i><i class="float"></i></div><figcaption><b>Compact desktop</b>Icon keys when the bar can't fit (and with more than 4 units below 1750px). In battle the roster moves to a card under the mini-map (below 1180px, or more than 4 units below 1160px).</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="panel"><div class="bu-mock full"><i class="map"></i><i class="dock l"></i><i class="dock r"></i><i class="float"></i></div><figcaption><b>Full screen</b>Header hidden. RADIO and AIM float as dock cards (54u header row, list / grid switch), the roster card sits under the mini-map. Full screen survives new games.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 11 MOTION & SOUND -->
  <section id="motion" class="bu-block">
    <div class="bu-head"><span class="eyebrow"><span class="index">11</span> MOTION &amp; SOUND</span><h2>Snappy keys, theatrical moments.</h2><p>Keys never spring. Springs are for pop-ins only. Reduced motion keeps every end state and drops the motion.</p></div>
    <div class="bu-table panel"><table><thead><tr><th>Motion</th><th>Timing</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>{motion.map(([a, b, c]) => <tr><td>{a}</td><td><code>{b}</code></td><td>{c}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="bu-table panel"><table><thead><tr><th>Sound cue</th><th>Character</th></tr></thead><tbody>{sounds.map(([a, b]) => <tr><td><code>{a}</code></td><td>{b}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
