      <div class="bu-iso-text"><span class="eyebrow">ISOLATION · SHADOW DOM</span><p>On someone else's site, mount the board in a shadow root: <code>mount(host, css, {"{"} palette {"}"})</code>. This box sits under a page rule that turns every button red with a dashed border. The board inside doesn't see it.</p></div>
      <div class="bu-hostile" data-shadow-demo aria-label="Board mounted in a shadow root"></div>
    </div>
    <ol class="bu-check panel">
      <li>Wrap the board in <code>&lt;div class="bui" data-theme data-side&gt;</code> and include the kit.</li>
      <li>Pass the palette; check every face reads with ink text on it.</li>
      <li>Map each action to a role colour; write labels as <b>WORD</b> · detail.</li>
      <li>Bar groups: per-unit radio · squad orders · roster · aim / mode · flag far right.</li>
      <li>Overlays: pause, result, stale page, with the sticker copy above.</li>
      <li>Launch keys use <code>launch()</code>; a reset never cancels the burst.</li>
      <li>Cards: grip, fold key, back tab, the placement rules.</li>
      <li>Comms toast placement per stage; tips mode.</li>
      <li>Boot screen and door hand-off if it ships as a full-game cartridge.</li>
      <li>Test 844×390, 1100, 1400, 1750, 1920 and full screen, both themes, both sides, 4 and 12 units.</li>
      <li>Reduced motion, keyboard and screen reader names; a size budget in CI.</li>
